<aside class="home-dict" aria-label="Dictionary entry for home">
  <p class="home-dict-lemma">
    <strong>home</strong>
    <span class="home-dict-pron">\ˈhōm\</span>
    <span class="home-dict-pos">n.</span>
    <span class="home-dict-pos">adj.</span>
    <span class="home-dict-pos">adv.</span>
    <span class="home-dict-pos">v.</span>
  </p>
  <p class="home-dict-etym">
    [ME <i>hom</i>, <i>ham</i>, fr. OE <i>hām</i> dwelling, estate, village; akin to OS <i>hēm</i>, OHG <i>heim</i>, ON <i>heimr</i> the world, Goth <i>haims</i> village. Cf. HAMLET. Bef. 12c.]
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>I.</b> <i>n.</i>
    <b>1 a</b> : the place where one lives permanently as a member of a family or household
    <span class="home-dict-ex">a house is not a ~</span>
    <b>b</b> : such a place regarded as the seat of domestic life, affection, and rest
    <span class="home-dict-ex">there is no place like ~</span>
    <b>c</b> : the family occupying such a place
    <b>2 a</b> : one’s native land or district
    <b>b</b> : the place of origin or natural habitat of a thing
    <b>3</b> : an institution providing residence and care
    <b>4</b> <i>Sports</i> : the goal that must be reached to score; <i>specif. Baseball</i> home plate
    <b>5</b> : the grave, conceived as a final abode
    <span class="home-dict-ex">gone to his last ~</span>
    <b>6</b> <i>Law</i> : domicile for jurisdiction, taxation, or suffrage.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>II.</b> <i>adj.</i>
    <b>1</b> : of or relating to the home or household
    <span class="home-dict-ex">~ cooking</span>
    <b>2</b> : made at home; not commercial
    <b>3</b> : of one’s own country, as distinguished from foreign
    <span class="home-dict-ex">the ~ team</span>
    <b>4</b> : reaching the mark; to the point
    <span class="home-dict-ex">a ~ truth</span>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>III.</b> <i>adv.</i>
    <b>1</b> : to or at home
    <span class="home-dict-ex">he went ~</span>
    <b>2</b> : to the heart of the matter; fully
    <span class="home-dict-ex">the charge struck ~</span>
    <b>3</b> : to one’s own country.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>IV.</b> <i>v. homed; homing</i>
    <i>intr.</i> <b>1</b> : to go or return home
    <b>2</b> : to proceed toward a destination by tracking a signal or landmark — often with <i>in</i>
    <span class="home-dict-ex">homed in on the real issue</span>
    <i>tr.</i> <b>1</b> : to send or bring home
    <b>2</b> : to provide with a home.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="home-dict-label">Idioms.</span>
    <b>at home</b> : in one’s house; at ease.
    <b>bring home</b> : to make unmistakably clear.
    <b>home free</b> : certain of success after difficulty.
    <b>make oneself at home</b> : to take one’s ease.
    <b>nothing to write home about</b> : unremarkable.
    <b>until the cows come home</b> : for a very long time.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="home-dict-label">Syn.</span>
    <b>Home</b>, <b>house</b>, <b>residence</b>, <b>abode</b>, <b>dwelling</b>.
    <i>House</i> names the building.
    <i>Residence</i> is formal.
    <i>Abode</i> is literary or legal.
    <i>Dwelling</i> is general.
    <i>Home</i> adds family, belonging, and rest.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="home-dict-label">Deriv.</span>
    homeless, homelike, homely, homemade, homemaker, homesick, homespun, homestead, homeward, homey.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="home-dict-label">Usage.</span>
    In careful use, <i>home</i> is not a genteel substitute for <i>house</i>. The house is the structure; the home is the life lived in it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="home-dict-label">Local.</span>
    <b>home</b> \ˈhōm\, <i>n.</i> <i>(Cheboygan Co., Mich.)</i> : <i>specif.</i> indoors, outdoors, and the river.
  </p>
</aside>
